From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: fall back to nl80211 mgmt frames when the monitor
 interface cannot be created

hostapd picks the monitor-interface path when the driver does not support
NL80211_CMD_PROBE_CLIENT or NL80211_FEATURE_SK_TX_STATUS.  Full-MAC drivers
such as aic8800 advertise a monitor interface mode but still refuse to
create one while a data/AP vif exists ("Monitor+Data interface support
(MON_DATA) disabled"), so nl80211_create_monitor_interface() fails with
-EOPNOTSUPP.

The compatibility fallback then set device_ap_sme = 1, which is wrong for
these drivers: they still drive the AP MLME from userspace.  setup_ap()
skipped both the monitor path and the nl80211 mgmt-frame subscription, so
hostapd transmitted beacons but never received a single auth/assoc frame -
clients could see the SSID and failed to associate.

Treat the missing monitor interface as "use NL80211_CMD_FRAME instead":
clear use_monitor and subscribe to the AP management frames.  A real
monitor-interface creation error (not -EOPNOTSUPP) still aborts setup.
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -6142,10 +6142,6 @@
 	if (!drv->device_ap_sme)
 		wpa_driver_nl80211_probe_req_report(bss, 0);
 
-	if (!drv->device_ap_sme && !drv->use_monitor)
-		if (nl80211_mgmt_subscribe_ap(bss))
-			return -1;
-
 	if (drv->device_ap_sme && !drv->use_monitor)
 		if (nl80211_mgmt_subscribe_ap_dev_sme(bss))
 			wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
@@ -6153,9 +6149,18 @@
 
 	if (!drv->device_ap_sme && drv->use_monitor &&
 	    nl80211_create_monitor_interface(drv) &&
-	    !drv->device_ap_sme)
+	    drv->use_monitor)
 		return -1;
 
+	/*
+	 * nl80211_create_monitor_interface() cleared use_monitor when the
+	 * driver refused the monitor interface (-EOPNOTSUPP): keep userspace
+	 * MLME and receive management frames over NL80211_CMD_FRAME.
+	 */
+	if (!drv->device_ap_sme && !drv->use_monitor)
+		if (nl80211_mgmt_subscribe_ap(bss))
+			return -1;
+
 	if (drv->device_ap_sme &&
 	    wpa_driver_nl80211_probe_req_report(bss, 1) < 0) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: Failed to enable "
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_monitor.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_monitor.c
@@ -385,14 +385,14 @@
 
 	if (drv->monitor_ifidx == -EOPNOTSUPP) {
 		/*
-		 * This is backward compatibility for a few versions of
-		 * the kernel only that didn't advertise the right
-		 * attributes for the only driver that then supported
-		 * AP mode w/o monitor -- ath6kl.
+		 * The driver advertises monitor mode but cannot create the
+		 * interface next to a data/AP vif (e.g. aic8800 full-MAC).
+		 * Keep userspace MLME and switch to management frames over
+		 * NL80211_CMD_FRAME instead of claiming device AP SME.
 		 */
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: Driver does not support "
 			   "monitor interface type - try to run without it");
-		drv->device_ap_sme = 1;
+		drv->use_monitor = 0;
 	}
 
 	if (drv->monitor_ifidx < 0)
